+# Star spline lap completion — 2026-10-06
+
+Owner report: laps on **star** could not complete, suggesting incorrectly generated spline checkpoints. Requirements: G01, R01, T01–T04, V03/V05, Q01, SP08 (spline corner gates accept legitimate inside lines while rejecting skipped sections).
+
+The report is reproduced and fixed. The generator recognized sharp joins between road pieces but overlooked sharp turns inside a smoothly fitted spline. On Star, straight gate planes beside a tight apex forced a legal inside line to double back through a small loop. A real recorded compact-car drive on the ordinary inside line completes **zero laps under the original gate generator and five under the corrected generator**, with identical car motion and no collisions. Restarting the race configures the corrected gates; no map edit is required.
+
+## Actual source and reproduction
+
+Read the owner's locally saved `track_26cfe6e8fd325084cceea883917357a7` document named Star. The saved original and WIP recovery copy contain the same three spline blocks and are byte-identical: SHA-256 `7cdf5918c75e332fd36b7231895eca8300ec649e0a8747eefbf7d87cbb056f35`. Both remain byte-identical after the work; neither was written, deleted or migrated. The exact owner-authored map is copied only into export-excluded `game/tests/fixtures/star_spline_lap.json` for regression. No public/shipping catalog entry is added.
+
+The circuit is approximately 400.589 m, with 496 compiled route points and 1,169 physical spline samples. Its centreline completed laps even before the repair. Naively offsetting that centreline also appeared to work, because offsets of a very tight bend fold back and cross the misplaced gate artificially. Removing only those small local offset loops produces a smooth inside line that stays on the actual road at every 0.2 m sample. Five of those eight on-road lines fail the original gate system, stuck at checkpoints 3, 13 or 16. That is the relevant failure, rather than a disconnected course or broken start line.
+
+## Implementation and versioning
+
+`TrackSession._road_corners` additionally recognizes tight turns at the spline's three internal interpolation knots. It uses the adjoining authored road directions to form a bisector gate, the actual width of that knot, the timed route direction and the existing miter/reach rules. Ordinary dense gates within that corner's corridor are omitted through the existing spacing mechanism. Star changes from **32 gates / 2 recognized corners to 19 gates / 11 recognized corners**. Every remaining gate still must be crossed in order; no automatic time penalty or shortcut credit is introduced.
+
+The implementation is deterministic and computed once when configuring a session. Car handling, physics version, road geometry/cells, spline points/widths, compiler22, start placement and visuals are unchanged. Opposite start-line direction is covered. Rules advance explicitly to **standing-5-road-gates-v19**, because checkpoint acceptance changes. Historical v18 boards are not rewritten or merged with v19 boards.
+
+The backend's existing explicit contract-upgrade adapter now derives v19 metadata and new race tickets from retained v12–v18 immutable revisions. Metadata and tickets use the same effective contract; rivalry eligibility recognizes those retained revisions when the active verifier is v19. Stored revision manifests, track IDs/share URLs and source documents remain unchanged. New attempts use a distinct v19 board hash, leaving historical PBs on their original boards. The compatibility matrix checks ownership/private metadata and both race and creator-test tickets. No database migration or score migration is added.
+
+## Actual verification
+
+Pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`, using `scripts/dev.ps1`. Windows desktop graphical captures use Compatibility/OpenGL on RTX 3090.
+
+- `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_star_spline_laps.gd`: final **59 checks, zero failures**. Five ordered centreline laps, five physical-spline laps, eight smooth on-road inside/outside offset lines, opposite start-line direction, ten actual infield corner cuts rejected, zero shortcut penalties, ordinary canonical-car five-lap driving and exact recording replay. The initial smooth-line regression had **five failures**, while the same centres/offsets with artificial loops still passed.
+- Standard compact diagnostic: **five laps / 37,173 ticks / zero contacts**, lap ticks `[7559, 7403, 7411, 7406, 7394]`. The first 36,000-tick diagnostic limit stopped late in lap five; expanded the diagnostic duration rather than altering checkpoint acceptance.
+- Real inside-line input generation uses a separate reference route only to choose quantized controls. Every physical/scored step uses the original compiled Star track. **Five laps / 39,658 ticks / zero contacts** under new rules; **zero laps / old missed checkpoint 3** for the exact same car motion with the actual task-start generator. No simulation state is teleported or altered to complete the race.
+- Both complete recordings were independently run through the real local `GodotVerifier.verify_run`, without submitting scores or accessing a live service. Inside-line lap ticks are `[8190, 7871, 7864, 7865, 7868]`; all five finish normally under rules19. Receipts and recordings are retained in evidence.
+- `... TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_star_spline_gates.gd -Graphical`: **5 checks, zero failures**. Actual before/after gate definitions at the problematic corner are rendered with the unchanged driving camera. These are paused diagnostic marker views, not fabricated race results. Screenshots inspected.
+- `... Validate -CommandTimeoutSeconds 600`: **315 scripts parse**, checkpoint rules **266**, notices **533**, bridge layers **259**, entries **258**, exits **2527**, creator **113**, road pieces **377**, editor workflow **252**, performance/equivalence **1215**, App **99**, and intervening handling/replay/surface/record/ghost/camera/catalog checks pass. The run then stops at the previously recorded unrelated menu-loading fixture: `TrackBrowser._show_detail` calls nonexistent `test_drivers_available` on `DelayedBoard`. **Full Validate is not reported green**; later components were not run. Existing ObjectDB cleanup warnings retained. Star's final expanded regression was also run separately; it is now included in Validate.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest backend/tests/test_verifier.py -q -x`: **64 passed** before adding the metadata compatibility adapter; retained recordings/timing assertions and the standalone canonical project pass under rules19.
+- Final broader backend `... -m pytest backend/tests/test_verifier.py backend/tests/test_review_reliability.py backend/tests/test_rivalry.py backend/tests/test_track_lifecycle.py -q -k 'not postgres' -x`: **121 passed / 1 skipped / 56 deselected**. Counts overlap the earlier batch. The additional legacy metadata/ticket upgrade matrix alone passes **24 cases**, preserving stored immutable manifests.
+- The first broader backend attempt reached **89 passed** then stopped on an unavailable inherited PostgreSQL test connection. No PostgreSQL success is claimed; the final batch deliberately selects disposable SQLite cases. A metadata test initially queried the public share endpoint for a private draft and got the correct 404; it now uses the owner's private `/me/tracks` endpoint without changing privacy behavior. Existing Starlette deprecation warning retained.
+- Scoped backend Ruff check passes after correcting import order; scoped `git diff --check` passes with line-ending normalization warnings only.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe docs/evidence/star-spline-laps-2026-10-06/create_checkpoint.py`: task-only checkpoint for **19 source/document files**. `git apply --reverse --check docs/evidence/star-spline-laps-2026-10-06/scoped-change.patch` exits **0**; the Git index and concurrent changes are untouched.
+
+## Files and evidence
+
+Runtime: `game/race/track_session.gd`, `race_rules.gd`; backend `contracts.py`, `tracks.py`, `rivalry.py`. Tests/contracts: `game/tests/test_checkpoint_rules.gd`, `test_bridge_exit_checkpoints.gd`; new `test_star_spline_laps.gd`, `capture_star_spline_gates.gd` and their UIDs / `fixtures/star_spline_lap.json`; `backend/tests/test_verifier.py`, `test_review_reliability.py`, `fixtures/verified_oval.json`; `scripts/dev.ps1`. The retained verified oval changes **only** its expected manifest's rules key; its document, inputs and timing assertions remain intact. Documentation: this file, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`.
+
+Evidence: `docs/evidence/star-spline-laps-2026-10-06/`, including [original corner gate](evidence/star-spline-laps-2026-10-06/before-first-corner.png), [corrected corner gate](evidence/star-spline-laps-2026-10-06/after-first-corner.png), full canonical recordings, backend verification receipts, actual command logs and task-start source snapshots. A task-only patch/normalized hashes provide the review checkpoint without staging concurrent work.
+
+## Remaining acceptance and rollout
+
+No phone attachment check, Android export/install or physical-device test was performed. Owner manual driving acceptance on Star and mobile gate-marker/performance acceptance remain. No live backend/cloud/NAS deployment, score submission, player-file rewrite or historical-board migration was performed. **Online races/creator verification need a matching rules19 API and verifier rollout**; the currently deployed rules18 build has not been updated by this task. The prepared metadata/ticket upgrade avoids copying or renaming retained tracks when that matching build is deployed. Existing tickets should be drained with their original matching workers before switching the active build; do not reinterpret old scored runs as v19. Local race/practice restarts immediately use the new gate generator.
